WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.800
Picture the shyest female friend, relative,
or loved one you know.

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.360
A real introvert.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:12.320
She can’t stand parties and playing the
dating game is her idea of a living hell.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.320
You won’t catch her dead in a bar.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:21.280
But imagine someday, everything changes: She’s
suddenly more relaxed, more outgoing.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:27.920
She goes out to parties and now you keep seeing
her with this one guy - again and again and

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:28.640
again.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:33.520
It seems like these days, all she does is
spend time with this guy.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:36.960
And to think, he’s never even introduced
himself to you.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.960
He’s practically a total stranger.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.960
But your friend seems happy enough, so it
doesn’t bother you.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:50.160
Until one day something strange happens: Your
friend just starts screaming.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.960
You can’t explain it, she can’t explain
it, her doctor can’t explain it.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:56.960
Nobody can explain it.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:02.320
All you know is that, for months on end, she
has involuntary screaming fits.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:04.320
Like something out of a nightmare.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:07.040
But still, she always smiles.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.400
She seems happy.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.720
As long as you don’t look at her eyes.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.360
There’s something oddly glassy about them.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:14.560
They seem plastic.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.000
Dead.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:23.440
Your friend is experiencing a dangerous phenomenon
known to the SCP Foundation as SCP - 3512,

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:28.640
an anomaly that only seems to affect women
between the ages of eighteen and forty.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:33.520
One woman is already dead as a result of this
and an additional nine others affected by

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:38.560
this strange anomaly have been catalogued
and contained in standard humanoid containment

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:39.920
chambers for study.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:45.600
At first, the Foundation couldn’t draw any
logical conclusions for why these women were

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:50.880
spontaneously experiencing total personality
changes and pronounced screaming fits.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:56.160
All the Foundation had to go on was that the
first cluster of infected individuals originated

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:58.080
in Barcelona, Spain.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:03.040
A Foundation facility in Boston dispatched
one of their best field operatives, Agent

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.960
Riley Cooper, on an investigative mission
to Barcelona.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.760
They wanted her to get to the bottom of this
phenomenon and put a stop to it before things

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.280
went any further.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:18.800
While in Spain, Agent Cooper would be assisted
by a local Foundation operative, Agent Tomàs

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.280
Rey, whose intimate knowledge of the locale&nbsp;

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:24.400
would provide a key advantage&nbsp;
in the investigation.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:29.200
Together, they’d crack this thing, and make
sure no other women were harmed.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:32.160
At least, that’s what the Foundation had
hoped.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:38.400
Instead, both agents disappeared under horrific
circumstances during the investigation.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:43.520
And today, we’re going to tell you about
the final days of Agent Cooper and Agent Rey,

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:50.000
and why attempting to investigate SCP-3512
was the last thing they ever did.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:56.080
Agent Cooper arrived on the fifteenth of July,
2016, and stepped out into the scorching summer

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:57.360
heat of Spain.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:02.400
Agent Cooper was everything you’d want in
a field operative for the Foundation: Intelligent,

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.640
dedicated, and professional.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:09.680
She rendezvoused with Agent Rey, who was a
comparatively smooth and laid-back figure.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:13.760
The two of them began their investigation
by speaking to the friends and families of

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.000
some of the infected women, pretending to&nbsp;

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:19.280
be doctors working for the&nbsp;
World Health Organization.

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:25.760
Agent Cooper, in her personal diaries, noted
how creepy and unreal the affected women seemed.

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:31.040
Most of the interviews were unnerving and
sad, but not exactly enlightening.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:37.040
However, as things drew to a close, a younger
sister of one of the victims mentioned a single

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:38.880
word “Blackout.”

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:43.680
Even the mention of the word caused the victim
to descend into another screaming fit.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:49.440
Agent Rey’s local knowledge came in handy
once again: He recognized the name, it was

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:51.360
a popular local nightclub.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:55.920
Agent Cooper and Agent Rey knew they had to
investigate the club, and went undercover

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:57.440
as regular patrons.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:02.480
For the first several hours they were there,
nothing happened, but then at 2:00 AM, a man

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:04.480
approached Agent Cooper at the bar.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:08.960
He was a tall, blond man with an unsettling
intensity to him.

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:13.840
He asked, without a hint of irony, what Agent
Cooper’s favorite star was.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:19.840
There was something off about this man - his
word choice was too precise, almost rehearsed.

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:22.000
He wasn’t drunk in the slightest.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:26.800
Agent Cooper intuited that this was the kind
of guy who liked to take advantage of women

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:27.760
in bars.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:32.560
When she threw a glance at Agent Rey, signalling
to him that something was off, the stranger

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:33.760
quickly left.

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:37.760
For Agent Cooper this only further confirmed
her suspicions.

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:42.400
The agents paid off the bouncer to find out
if the tall stranger was a regular, and then

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:43.760
what his name was.

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:48.560
After being slipped some cash, the bouncer
was all too eager to share.

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:52.240
The strange man came here all the time, and
he knew his name too.

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:54.320
It was Josep Oriol

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:59.520
Agent Cooper and Agent Rey wasted no time
in finding Josep Oriol’s apartment and receiving

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:03.200
authorization to perform a comprehensive search
on the premises.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:07.600
And as soon as they did, they found cause
to declare the man a Person of Interest in

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:10.640
the SCP-3512 investigation.

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:16.160
The apartment was a smorgasbord of suspicious
activity: Oriol was a software developer,

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:18.560
but he had extensive records on the architecture&nbsp;

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:21.920
of the local area - including&nbsp;
buildings, utilities,

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.520
and railway tunnels.

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:27.840
Josep correctly figured the investigators
were coming for him, and had fled his home

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:29.600
before they could get there.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:32.240
And this was only the tip of the iceberg.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:37.040
Agents Cooper and Rey then found a book with
a plain cover sitting on Oriol’s kitchen

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:41.840
table - Cooper thought it was a publisher’s
proof, a kind of pre-publication prototype

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:42.960
copy of a book.

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:48.480
They collected it but didn’t read it straightaway,
worrying about its potentially cognitohazardous

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:49.200
nature.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:54.480
And besides, they were a little distracted
by the home-made monstrosity sitting next

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:55.120
to it.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:06:00.720
It looked to Agent Cooper like a sculpted
blob of wax, with a series of twelve makeshift

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:08.720
legs made from a variety of substances including
Lego pieces, rose stems, a crab claw, a corkscrew.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:13.440
Rey called Cooper into the bathroom, where
there were a number of boxes filled with similar

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:18.960
supplies: Bodkins, quills, doll's limbs, wire,
and syringes.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:24.000
When Cooper led Rey back into the kitchen
to see Oriol’s little art project, later

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:30.880
classified by the Foundation as SCP-3512-1,
they were surprised and unnerved to see that

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:32.720
it was already gone.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:36.080
Everything about this&nbsp;
situation screamed “anomalous”,&nbsp;

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:38.800
and it only got worse later that night, when

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:43.760
Cooper actually read the book she’d collected
from Oriol’s apartment, being sure to wear

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:46.960
cognitohazard-filtering goggles as a precaution.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:52.560
The book, now known to the&nbsp;
Foundation as SCP-3512-2,&nbsp;

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:55.680
was entitled “The More You Know: A Pick-Up

00:06:55.680 --> 00:07:00.560
Artist’s Bible”, and was written by a
man using the pen name “Enigma.”

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:07.280
As the title suggests, it was a misogynistic,
625 page non-fiction book on the subject of

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:08.480
picking up women.

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:13.520
It even had a foreword on its effectiveness
by popular American rapper Calvin Broadus

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:19.840
Jr., better known as Snoop Dogg, though after
being contacted by the Foundation, Mr. Dogg

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:21.840
claimed no knowledge of the book.

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:26.720
The book began with your typical creepy and
dehumanizing seduction tactics for the first

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:31.920
eleven chapters, but the following twelve
chapters which were each entitled “Chapter

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:37.680
Twelve” delved into increasingly creepy
and esoteric techniques including advanced

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:43.920
geometric proofs, the interpretation of dreams,
do-it-yourself surgical techniques, symbolism

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:46.960
in architecture, and anomalous rituals.

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:52.640
The book's afterword is composed of more than
15,000 anagrams of the book's title, laid

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:55.840
out in spiral and triangular patterns.

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:58.480
Cooper took a particular morbid interest in&nbsp;

00:07:58.480 --> 00:08:01.760
Chapter 18, where it appeared&nbsp;
to provide instructions

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:08.960
on creating objects that looked like the anomalous
SCP-3512-1 sculptures found in Oriel’s apartment.

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:09.840
The chapter read:

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:15.520
“Make a rough ball of the materials you've
harvested, and place it in the freezer for

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:17.360
6-12 hours.

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:20.560
Pork fat can be used, but&nbsp;
will have less satisfactory&nbsp;

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:21.520
results.

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:22.800
Who knew, right?

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:25.440
While you wait, you can prepare the limbs.

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:28.560
Concentrate on articulation rather than strength.

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:34.240
You may want to add simple tools to some limbs,
if the object of your desire is more careful

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:40.080
than most, but remember that the more complicated
you make them, the more precise your sculpting

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:40.880
will need to be.

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:45.200
Lay your prepared limbs out on a clean, flat
surface.

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:49.920
Once your adipose preparation has had time
to freeze, carefully carve it into the shape

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:51.840
you learned in Chapter Twelve.

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:55.600
You will know it is ready when you see it
start smiling at you.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:09:00.320
Now introduce the limbs - they should "take"
almost immediately.

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:05.600
Wait until your intended is likely to be sleeping,
then concentrate your thoughts on her face,

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:09.360
and particularly the inside of her mouth and
throat.

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:15.920
Soon you'll see your new friend scurry off,
ready to help you establish social dominance...”

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:20.800
If this wasn’t disturbing enough, the next
chapter advised the using scissors in the

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:26.160
removal of the aspiring-seductionist’s pinkie
finger, as well as the pinkie fingers of their

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:30.000
family members, to help increase their seductive
power.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:34.560
It appeared to Cooper that these rituals and
seemingly living anomalous sculptures were

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:41.120
behind the SCP-3512 phenomena, and that night,
they got their next break in the case.

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:44.960
The two agents had sent the architectural
plans found in Oriol’s apartment back to

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:50.240
Foundation HQ, and while most of it was found
to be public records of the local area, there

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:56.800
was one notable abnormality: A secret exit
in a little used subway tunnel that led to

00:09:56.800 --> 00:10:03.920
a grand spiral staircase, heading down to...Well,
they just didn’t know, and if was the job

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:07.040
of Agents Cooper and Rey to find out.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:11.440
They set out later that night, on what they
didn’t know would be the last mission they’d

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:12.400
ever take...

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:17.840
The two agents descended the spiral staircase
for what felt like hours until they reached

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:20.480
an elaborate system of tunnels at the bottom.

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:25.200
They began exploring the tunnels and found
that they were cramped, and covered in strange,

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:27.040
ritualistic carvings.

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:31.680
Occasionally, they even saw clusters of human
pinkie fingers sticking out of the wall.

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:37.200
They kept going and soon found that whatever
they were moving towards was loud, immensely

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:40.960
hot, and the smell was truly horrific.

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:46.640
As the almost deafening mechanical drone got
louder and louder and the smell grew worse,

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:50.400
they knew they must be getting closer to whatever
was happening here.

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:50.720
.

00:10:50.720 --> 00:10:57.040
The tunnel soon opened up into a giant chamber
where they found something horrific.

00:10:57.040 --> 00:11:01.680
In front of them was what looked to be an
entire river of bubbling, liquid human fat

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:07.840
- the exact kind that the author Enigma had
recommenced using to create the mind-altering

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:12.000
SCP-3512-1 sculptures in his book.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:17.520
And speaking of the book, across the river
Agent Cooper and Agent Rey noticed a complex

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:23.680
series of printing presses, presumably churning
out more copies of “The More You Know: A

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:29.040
Pick-Up Artist’s Bible” to spread its
anomalous influence far and wide.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:33.600
However, before the duo could literally stop
the presses, they were attacked.

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:39.840
A huge 3512-1 entity with legs made out of
human spines, jumped down from the ceiling.

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:44.880
It latched onto Agent Cooper, embedding her
in its waxy body and dragging her into the

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:46.880
disgusting river of hot fat.

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:53.520
Agent Rey was separated and lost in the tunnels;
presumed dead, as he hasn’t been seen since.

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:58.320
Agent Cooper, however, would live to see a
far more horrifying fate.

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:02.960
She was carried downriver by the greasy tide
until her body was washed up in a different

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:08.640
chamber that looked to be a place of worship
below the Sagrada Familia Basilica, filled

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:12.560
with thousands of tiny, crawling 3512-1s.

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:20.240
There, she met the creator of all this: A
horrific thing that was perhaps once a man,

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:24.640
now covered in wriggling, living pinkie fingers
sticking out of its body.

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:28.160
It was disgusting, but she wouldn’t mind
for long.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:33.520
WIn fact, the next time Cooper woke up, she
didn’t have a problem with it at all.

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:37.120
She was changed, just like all the others.

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:41.120
Another victim of the SCP-3512 phenomenon.

00:12:41.120 --> 00:12:47.040
She was giggly, outgoing, and uninhibited,
all despite the nightmarish situation she

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:47.840
was in.

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:51.120
She loved the horrifying monster that had
done this to her.

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:52.960
She didn’t have a choice not to.

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:57.840
And when he was tired of her, he took her
and threw her down into a large pit in his

00:12:57.840 --> 00:13:00.240
chamber, the same one where the many dead&nbsp;

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:03.280
bodies of his previous&nbsp;
mind-controlled “girlfriends”

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:04.240
were laying.

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:06.880
Neither Agent was ever seen again after this.

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:12.160
Mobile Task Force Zeta-9, aka "Mole Rats",
have been sent into the tunnels to investigate,

00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:16.560
but they didn’t find any of the locations
comparable to the ones seen by Cooper and

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:18.320
Rey in their last hours.

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:21.840
Whoever did all this is still out there.

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:23.680
Still dangerous.

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:29.120
So ladies, if ever you see a guy you know
reading a copy of “The More You Know: A

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:35.200
Pick-Up Artist’s Bible”, run like your
life and sanity depends on it - because this

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:38.560
time, it really, really does.

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:46.240
Now go check out “SCP - 001 - The Children
- Ouroborous Cycle” and “SCP - 4999 - Someone

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:52.720
To Watch Over Us Tale” for more records
of mysterious phenomena from the SCP Foundation.

